{
  "configuration_id": "config_010",
  "reason": "Evidence: Only one experiment (config_001: rna_only, singleprofile, pca_n2000) has been completed, yielding a low validation accuracy of ~48.5% and F1 of ~46.4%, establishing a weak RNA-only baseline. This leaves the most critical design question unanswered: does the image modality carry meaningful predictive signal for this task? Question being tested: config_010 (image_only, singleprofile, resnet50) directly measures the standalone performance of the image modality with a well-established encoder, providing a second modality-specific baseline. Why this is the best next experiment: Before investing budget in multimodal fusion or more complex RNA encoders, we must know whether images are a viable signal source. If image_only performs comparably or better than RNA-only, multimodal configurations become the clear exploitation target. If it performs poorly, we redirect budget toward improving the RNA side (better encoders like scgpt, multiprofile aggregation). This single experiment maximally reduces uncertainty about the highest-level architectural decision (which modality to rely on) and will most efficiently guide all subsequent experiments under the limited budget."
}

